{comment: Verse 1}
[G]A lame man was sitting [G7]outside the gate Begging [C]alms of those [G]who entered in
[G]Peter and John came [Em]upon him The [A]lame man was expecting from [D]them
[G]Peter said silver and gold [G7]have I none But such as [C]I have I give [A7]unto thee
That's when the [C]Spirit touched the [D]lame man
He [G]leaped to his [C]feet crying "[D]Look what He's done for [G]me"

{comment: Verse 2}
[G]I was bound by the chains of [G7]darkness and [C]sin I had [G]no hope, no peace of mind
[G]My sins were as scarlet He washed them white as [Em]snow
He [A]opened up my blinded [D]eyes
[G]Now my soul does rejoice Since I [G7]made Him my choice
I've got [C]love, peace, everything I [A7]need
My [C]name's been written [D]down in the [G]Lambs book of [C]life
Can't [D]you see what He's done for [G]me!
